From 23eec8dc3d7ed2c88e5f8f61b3ab4bc920c646c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 15:12:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00832/11362] [outer-loop] Thesis doc: #4 v2 --
 energy-as-teacher is HEADROOM-bounded (gold UB also flat)

Fixed harness (deep-sup + anchor + K=32): certified yield 4.6%->62.9%, no collapse.
Yet energy gives no lift AND the gold upper bound also fails to beat base (-1.4%) --
the base is gold-saturated (converged), so NO headroom for any teacher. P0.1 lesson
again: energy's generative value is gated by headroom everywhere. Only the in-loop
gate (#3, +1.8% robust) survives as a generative contribution (inference-time error
pruning, not teaching).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
